# hello: the smallest app built entirely on CuBit (SELF-002), its manifest
# step included (tests/device-builds: no step answered from the host).
# It says hello on its greeting outlet, in a log record and on the kernel
# console, then exits 0. Its outlet gives it a program description, so a
# console whose launch table admits it (the staged builds,
# tests/console-run-staged) offers it as the CCL interface hello:
# (hello.run (Hello_Parameters)), its text in (hello.com.cubit.hello.greeting r).
(Executable_Manifest
  identity => "com.cubit.hello"
  version => "0.1.0"
  requests => [(service "logstore" "logstore")]
  outlets => [(Outlet "com.cubit.hello.greeting" Element.Text pages => 1)])
